  "body": "Prompt logprobs previously allocated chunk result buffers, scanned ranks separately and concatenated three outputs. This patch writes final slices and fuses ranks into the selected-score pass, preserving exact score/rank bits and native ID layouts.\n\nAll 10 prompt GPU timing cases pass a zero-margin gate on both boots. Two predeclared precision extensions pass independently and pooled; the full-vocabulary log-probability case is about 32% faster. Two focused boots pass 76 tests each; the combined suite passes 1,167 tests twice. All 120 unaffected normal score programs retain their qualified code and bindings.\n\nStacked on #895. Fresh patch application reproduces the recorded tree; doctor and diff checks pass. Built-image, full model and physical-fabric qualification remain release gates. No serving runtime or promoted configuration changes. Raw evidence, including unsuccessful variants, is retained on `feat/tilelang-runtime-closure`; this patch's six files match that source byte-for-byte.\n",
